Z||000000||Cooter||12-19-1999||07:47 PM||||I finally got the coolant pipe replaced on my "new" 88 GT and deciced to run a compression test on it to see how bad off the engine was-it has 179,000 miles showing on the odometer. I only checked the "easy" cylinders and the readings were 145, 150 and 150 psi on a warm engine and throttle opened. Is this normal, low or what? The engine doesnt make excessive noises or smoke. So what should I do?||||reg||5
